00:50:54.142 --> 00:50:56.382
So why is train why is RL training of robotic

00:50:56.382 --> 00:50:58.432
foundation models a challenge? Why can't

00:50:58.432 --> 00:51:00.552
we just use everything that we've already,

00:51:00.792 --> 00:51:02.571
figured out how to use for,

00:51:02.811 --> 00:51:04.591
LLMs and other kinds of systems?

00:51:05.462 --> 00:51:07.762
Well, the trouble is that if

00:51:08.002 --> 00:51:10.232
the you want to do reinforcement learning

00:51:10.232 --> 00:51:12.472
training for robots and you want to do it on top of pre

00:51:12.472 --> 00:51:14.702
trained models, there's a very good chance,

00:51:14.702 --> 00:51:16.727
and this is not a this is not an obvious statement, but I think there's

00:51:16.728 --> 00:51:18.932
a very good chance that you're gonna want to do it on top of pre trained models, it in the real

00:51:18.932 --> 00:51:20.051
world. Why?

00:51:20.972 --> 00:51:23.392
Well, because if the whole

00:51:23.392 --> 00:51:25.731
