01:18:08.602 --> 01:18:10.811
the a big part of why they're different is that

01:18:11.211 --> 01:18:13.531
when you when you use AWR, what you're really

01:18:13.532 --> 01:18:15.852
doing is importance waiting. And importance

01:18:15.852 --> 01:18:17.792
weighting can be very bad for big models,

01:18:18.412 --> 01:18:20.912
Why? Well, because big models are kind of notorious

01:18:21.211 --> 01:18:23.542
for learning the right answer, but not being

01:18:23.542 --> 01:18:25.691
well calibrated. And if you're using importance weighting

01:18:25.691 --> 01:18:27.901
where you really want the action probabilities to

01:18:27.901 --> 01:18:30.061
reflect their frequencies, then you want a model

01:18:30.062 --> 01:18:32.092
that's well calibrated. And big networks

01:18:32.092 --> 01:18:34.481
are just not that good at that. So essentially,

01:18:34.782 --> 01:18:36.812
with AWR, even a bad

01:18:36.812 --> 01:18:38.852
action appears as a good action

01:18:38.852 --> 01:18:41.002
with a small weight. And if the model is

01:18:41.002 --> 01:18:43.171
really smart about learning the right probability

01:18:43.171 --> 01:18:45.331
on that, it will actually say it's low probability. But if it

01:18:45.332 --> 01:18:47.692
just if it's big and it fits everything, even

01:18:47.972 --> 01:18:50.081
the bad action will actually end up being fitted very well.

01:18:50.322 --> 01:18:52.722
Whereas with the optimality condition, you're explicitly telling

01:18:52.722 --> 01:18:54.872
it like, hey, this is an action, you should learn

01:18:54.872 --> 01:18:57.122
about it, but remember, what you should learn is that it's bad

01:18:57.282 --> 01:18:59.441
This is an example of what not to do. And if you just

01:18:59.441 --> 01:19:01.512
think about what c f

01:19:01.512 --> 01:19:03.802
g does when you're running it for sampling, It

01:19:04.362 --> 01:19:06.102
actually pushes you away from

01:19:06.562 --> 01:19:08.677
the unconditional generation.

01:19:09.332 --> 01:19:11.602
So anything that is labeled

01:19:11.602 --> 01:19:13.722
as good you'll be you'll push towards it and away

01:19:13.722 --> 01:19:15.901
from the other stuff. So that's actually very

01:19:15.901 --> 01:19:17.981
good for sharpening distribution around specifically the

01:19:17.981 --> 01:19:20.322
good actions. Thank you very much.

