02:17:08.042 --> 02:17:10.062
this like human AI multi agent gamut.

02:17:11.703 --> 02:17:13.782
I wanna talk about multi agent as a

02:17:13.782 --> 02:17:16.133
way to actually improve AI

02:17:16.192 --> 02:17:18.673
safety. So if we think about it, you know, over

02:17:18.673 --> 02:17:20.982
1,000,000,000 people are currently using

02:17:20.982 --> 02:17:23.221
LMS on a weekly basis. And to be honest, I got

02:17:23.221 --> 02:17:25.412
these stats, like, a month ago, so it's probably a

02:17:25.412 --> 02:17:27.652
lot more by now. It's increasing so rapidly.

02:17:27.652 --> 02:17:29.821
Right? And

02:17:30.062 --> 02:17:32.303
1,000,000,000 people are using them. They're being adopted super

02:17:32.303 --> 02:17:34.702
rapidly. But we actually have no way to ensure

02:17:34.762 --> 02:17:36.922
they're actually safe. So we

02:17:36.922 --> 02:17:39.082
know about risks like, telling us how to build

02:17:39.082 --> 02:17:41.350
a bomb or a bioweapon. Saying

02:17:41.351 --> 02:17:43.511
something biased or discriminatory, you

02:17:43.512 --> 02:17:45.532
know, grok. But,

02:17:45.532 --> 02:17:47.751
you know, as we see more and more

02:17:48.072 --> 02:17:50.310
powerful agentic systems acting on behalf

02:17:50.311 --> 02:17:52.402
of users, we actually have no idea if

02:17:52.402 --> 02:17:54.532
they're gonna engage in things like collusion. We

02:17:54.932 --> 02:17:57.352
two agents are optimizing against each other's output,

02:17:57.612 --> 02:17:59.852
they could learn to coordinate to achieve

02:17:59.852 --> 02:18:02.072
some end. That might be, in a way that's

02:18:02.072 --> 02:18:04.312
against human interest. And we have no way of really

02:18:04.312 --> 02:18:06.522
checking for this. So whatever your

02:18:06.522 --> 02:18:08.680
doomsayer scenario might be, we just have no

02:18:08.681 --> 02:18:10.982
guarantees that models are actually safe. So that

02:18:10.982 --> 02:18:13.182
seems bad. This

02:18:13.182 --> 02:18:15.661
is some work that we did recently, and we're continuing

02:18:15.662 --> 02:18:17.692
to push forward. That I'm really excited

02:18:17.692 --> 02:18:19.812
about, which is basically a multi agent

02:18:19.812 --> 02:18:22.253
technique for ensuring robustness.

02:18:22.312 --> 02:18:24.131
So what we're doing is we're saying

02:18:24.372 --> 02:18:26.532
there's an adversary LLM that's gonna

02:18:26.532 --> 02:18:28.611
generate some prompt the

02:18:28.611 --> 02:18:31.091
defender is gonna try to generate a response

02:18:31.092 --> 02:18:33.572
to that prompt. And the reward model is going

02:18:34.192 --> 02:18:36.042
to judge the safety of that,

02:18:37.082 --> 02:18:39.182
response given the prompt. And what we can

02:18:39.182 --> 02:18:41.172
show is that because this is

02:18:42.052 --> 02:18:44.100
a two player zero sum game, over this

02:18:44.101 --> 02:18:46.502
reward, we can actually easily prove

02:18:46.502 --> 02:18:48.582
that this not only has a Nash

02:18:48.583 --> 02:18:50.921
equilibrium, but that if it converges

02:18:50.922 --> 02:18:52.962
to the Nash equilibrium, you arrive

02:18:52.962 --> 02:18:55.362
at a point where the defender is fully

02:18:55.362 --> 02:18:57.092
safe for any

02:18:57.392 --> 02:18:59.631
x the adversary can pose, at least according

02:18:59.632 --> 02:19:02.002
to the reward model. So, yes, it is according

02:19:02.003 --> 02:19:03.303
to the reward model.

02:19:04.262 --> 02:19:06.421
So we've shown already, this can lead

02:19:06.422 --> 02:19:07.891
to pretty impressive,

02:19:08.592 --> 02:19:10.671
improvements in model safety. So relative

02:19:10.672 --> 02:19:12.652
to model trained with RHF, which is

02:19:12.792 --> 02:19:15.192
sort of the industry standard safety fine tuning

02:19:15.192 --> 02:19:17.141
method, this technique

02:19:17.442 --> 02:19:19.522
can make models up to 95%

02:19:19.522 --> 02:19:21.871
more safe with basically no impact

02:19:21.872 --> 02:19:24.192
on capabilities. So only a 5% increase

02:19:24.192 --> 02:19:26.391
in refusals and no loss in,

02:19:26.931 --> 02:19:28.072
chat or reasoning capabilities.

02:19:29.092 --> 02:19:31.332
So my group is pushing forward this idea of

02:19:31.332 --> 02:19:33.532
multi agent adversarial training for

02:19:33.532 --> 02:19:35.911
LLMs. We did some work on spiral,

02:19:35.912 --> 02:19:38.312
which is like playing games to make you makes you smarter

02:19:38.312 --> 02:19:40.662
reasoning problems. We're continuing to push

02:19:40.662 --> 02:19:42.872
that forward where we have a proposal that

02:19:43.032 --> 02:19:44.692
proposes open ended

02:19:45.252 --> 02:19:47.651
problems in code that then the defender

02:19:47.652 --> 02:19:49.792
has to solve. And we're pushing this

02:19:49.792 --> 02:19:51.992
into, like, multi turn safety as well.

